            <ArticleTitle>Melorheostosis of the humerus: a rare differential diagnosis of carpal tunnel syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>125-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.main.2010.01.003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Melorheostosis is an uncommon and rare linear hyperostosis, which can be complicated by soft tissue changes. We present a case of this disorder in the humerus, clinically referred because of carpal tunnel syndrome. Although treatment is usually conservative, in this case, a neurolysis and resection of the sclerotic bone were done with good clinical result.</AbstractText>
